      "title": "Regional Manager",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002178 Date posted 08/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 29/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£44,746 - £50,253) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002178.pdf Regional Manager Job description Leeds Beckett University is looking for a dynamic leader to join our International Recruitment and Partnerships team. The Regional Manager, focussing on East and South East Asia, is a pivotal management position within the International Recruitment and Partnerships leadership team. The region represents a significant proportion of our international student recruitment activity including a number of emerging / developing markets. The Region is also a strategic focus for our Transnational Education (TNE) development and currently accounts for significant tuition fee income through active partnerships. We are looking for someone with significant experience of working in a Higher Education Institution or similar, with specific professional knowledge/experience of international student recruitment and partnership development. You will provide an excellent customer service for students, parents, agents, partners and other stakeholders and some overseas travel may be required. For further information, please contact Tom Kyle, Head of International Recruitment and Partnerships at t.a.kyle@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing Date: Thursday 29th October 2026 at 23:29 Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
