      "title": "Academic Quality Support Officer - Fixed term to 29/10/27",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002176 Date posted 07/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 26/10/2026 Location Blank Salary Grade 4 (£30,378 - £34,610) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ2176.pdf Academic Quality Support Officer - Fixed term to 29/10/27 Job description Are you incredibly organised with great attention to detail? Are you looking for a busy role in a friendly team? Leeds Business School are looking to appoint a flexible and enthusiastic Academic Quality Support Officer. This is a hybrid working role, based partly at City Campus and partly from home. You will be able to provide high quality, operational and strategic support to academic and administrative colleagues, as well as external stakeholders. We are looking for candidates who can support Leeds Beckett’s diverse student community to achieve excellent outcomes, by maintaining robust quality processes such as revalidation, annual monitoring and review, academic integrity and module evaluation. Leeds Beckett is committed to creating and maintaining a safe, welcoming and inclusive community which nurtures a culture of respect and consideration for all. We encourage applications from people from all backgrounds and aim to have a workforce that represents the student body and wider society that we serve. Closing Date: Monday 26th October 2026 (23.59) Interview Date: Monday 16th November (this may be subject the change) To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Gareth Robertshaw at G.Robertshaw@leedsbeckett.ac.uk Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
