    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=108292OJCz&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Food Services Supervisor (Full time, 40 weeks, Term Time only)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002173 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,378 - £34,610 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002173.pdf Food Services Supervisor (Full time, 40 weeks, Term Time only) Job description We are looking for an enthusiastic, experienced and customer-focused Food Services Supervisor to join our busy Food Services team within Estates and Facilities working across both City & Headingley Campus. As Food Services Supervisor, you will play a key role in the day-to-day organisation and delivery of food, retail and hospitality services across the University. Working closely with the Food Services Manager, you will supervise and support a team of General Assistants, ensuring that our services operate safely, efficiently and to consistently high standards. You will be responsible for coordinating staffing and workloads, including rota planning and the management of sessional and casual staff, while ensuring that our customers receive an excellent service. You will also take a hands-on approach to resolving customer queries and complaints, supporting colleagues and maintaining a welcoming environment for students, staff, conference delegates and visitors. This is a varied role where no two days are necessarily the same. You will support food, retail and hospitality activity across the University, including internal and external events, and will contribute to initiatives designed to improve customer experience, sales and service delivery. About you You will have proven experience of supervising and line managing staff within a fast-paced food retail, hospitality or similar customer-facing environment. You will be confident leading a team, allocating workloads and maintaining high standards of customer service, food safety and health and safety. You will have a minimum Level 3 Food Safety Certificate, or equivalent, together with a sound understanding of workplace health and safety requirements, including COSHH, manual handling and fire awareness. Experience of using food service procurement and EPOS systems, including analysing sales information and maintaining accurate allergen and product information, would be advantageous. About the team Food Services is an important part of the student and staff experience at Leeds Beckett University, providing food, retail and hospitality services across our campuses. You will join a team committed to delivering safe, high-quality and customer-focused services. You will work collaboratively with colleagues across Estates and Facilities and will have the opportunity to contribute to the continued development of our food, retail and hospitality offer. The role will also provide the opportunity to deputise for the Food Services Manager when required, giving you valuable experience in supporting the wider operation. Why join us? You will also have opportunities to develop your skills and knowledge through training, continuing professional development and experience across the University's food, retail and hospitality services. Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=372596OJCz&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Performance Services Manager",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002171 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£44,746 - £50,253) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002171.pdf Performance Services Manager Job description Could you lead the programme that helps talented student athletes reach their potential? We're looking for a Performance Services Manager to head up strength and conditioning, performance support services and coaching across Leeds Beckett's performance sport programmes. Beckett Sport delivers sport and physical activity for students, colleagues and the wider Leeds community, from recreational sessions right through to performance sport. Our performance offer supports athletes on our Focus Sports, University Sport Scholarship, TASS and Talent Hub programmes, backed by a dedicated team of S&C coaches, physiotherapy and specialist coaching staff. Reporting to the Head of Beckett Sport, you'll lead a team that includes our Performance Sport Co-ordinator, Assistant Strength and Conditioning Coach, Performance Sport Physiotherapist, Rugby Programme Manager and Head Coach Netball. You will: • Lead and develop our S&C and support services, making sure athletes get high-quality individual and group programmes across a range of sports and training environments. • Work closely with the sports medicine team to manage, treat and prevent injuries. • Manage our external partnerships, including TASS, UKAD Clean Sport, National Governing Bodies and local professional clubs, and represent Beckett Sport internally and externally. • Build strong links with academic and research colleagues to create placements, mentoring and vocational learning that improve our students' employability. • Plan and manage budgets, review services against best practice and act on customer feedback, deputising for the Head of Beckett Sport when needed. What we're looking for: • UKSCA accreditation, with experience of leading a comprehensive performance sport and S&C programme, including for student athletes. • A track record of planning, delivering and monitoring S&C for high-performance athletes as part of a multi-disciplinary team. • Strong communication and influencing skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with managers, coaches and partners. • Good organisation and project management skills, a service-focused approach and a genuine commitment to your own professional development. Beckett Sport operates seven days a week, so some evening and weekend work will be needed in line with training and competition schedules. If you're ready to shape how performance sport is delivered at Leeds Beckett, we'd love to hear from you. In your application, please show how you meet the criteria in the Employee Specification. The role is based at Headingley Campus. The role is fully campus based, a vibrant community of both students and colleagues. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Mark Dunstan at m.dunstan@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=378569OJCo&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Quantity Surveyor",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002168 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 (£39,906 - £44,746) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support, Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002168.pdf Quantity Surveyor Job description Leeds Beckett University is seeking an experienced and commercially focused Quantity Surveyor to join our Estates and Facilities team. This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in the commercial management and delivery of the University's capital and revenue projects. Working across a diverse portfolio of estates activities, you will provide professional quantity surveying, procurement, contract management and commercial assurance services, helping to ensure projects are delivered effectively, efficiently and with strong financial and commercial control. You will work closely with project managers, consultants, contractors, professional advisers and colleagues across the University, providing expert advice on cost, procurement, contracts and risk. You will be instrumental in identifying and resolving commercial and contractual issues, supporting informed decision-making and helping to deliver positive outcomes for the University and its stakeholders. We are looking for a qualified or professionally developing Quantity Surveyor with strong experience of working within a construction, estates or property environment. You will have: • A first degree in Quantity Surveying or another relevant subject, together with membership of an appropriate professional body or evidence that you are working towards professional membership. • Strong commercial awareness and the ability to identify, assess and mitigate financial and contractual risks. • Excellent planning and organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet tight deadlines across multiple projects. • Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with colleagues, consultants, contractors and senior stakeholders. This role offers the opportunity to work within a varied and challenging estates environment, contributing directly to the University's ongoing development and investment in its estate. You will have the opportunity to work on a diverse range of projects and services, collaborate with a wide range of professional and operational colleagues, and make a tangible contribution through effective commercial management, procurement and project delivery. We are looking for someone who can combine technical quantity surveying expertise with excellent communication, commercial judgement and a strong commitment to delivering high-quality services. If you are an experienced Quantity Surveyor looking for an opportunity to apply your expertise within a dynamic university environment, we would welcome your application. Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=645068OJCz&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Business Services Administrator",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002170 Date posted 05/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 3 (£26,093 - £30,378) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002170.pdf Business Services Administrator Job description At Leeds Beckett University, our Estates and Facilities teams play an important role in creating an environment where our students, staff and visitors can thrive. We are looking for a Business Services Administrator to join our Business Support & Governance team and provide a professional, responsive, and customer-focused administrative service across Estates and Facilities. This is a varied role where you will be at the heart of our day-to-day service. You will work with colleagues across the University, as well as students, visitors, contractors, and suppliers, helping to make sure enquiries are dealt with efficiently and our services run smoothly. You will provide support across our Estates and Facilities helpdesks, University switchboard, car parking administration, and wider business support activities. You will also maintain accurate information across our systems, organise meetings, prepare documentation and support colleagues with a range of administrative activities. If you enjoy working with people, are organised and can manage a varied workload, this could be the role for you. You will provide a professional and customer-focused service, acting as an important link between our customers and Estates and Facilities service teams. We are looking for an organised, approachable, and proactive administrator who takes pride in delivering a high-quality service. You will have experience of working in an administrative role and be confident using Microsoft Office and databases to enter, maintain and retrieve information. Along with good interpersonal and communication skills, the ability to build positive relationships with a wide range of people and the confidence to use your own initiative. At Leeds Beckett, our people are central to creating an inclusive, supportive, and welcoming University community. As part of our Estates and Facilities team, you will work with colleagues across the University and have the opportunity to develop your knowledge and experience in a varied administrative role. You will be part of a team that supports the University environment every day – helping our campuses operate effectively and providing the services our students, staff and visitors rely on. We value people who are committed to delivering excellent customer service, working collaboratively, and looking for ways to improve what we do. Leeds Beckett University is a vibrant and diverse community based in the heart of Leeds. We are committed to creating an environment where everyone feels valued, respected, and able to contribute. We recognise the different experiences, skills, and perspectives that our people bring and the contribution they make to our university. Whatever your role, you will have the opportunity to make a difference to the experience of our students, staff, and wider University community. Closing date: Monday 19th October 2026 (23:59) Please be advised that due to the minimum salary thresholds imposed by the UKVI, this post will not qualify for university sponsorship for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. You must have the right to work in the UK to apply for this vacancy. Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
