      "title": "Academic Quality Enhancement Officer (Fixed term to 30/11/27)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002166 Date posted 01/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 13/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 \n(£39,906 - 44,746 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002166.pdf Academic Quality Enhancement Officer (Fixed term to 30/11/27) Job description We are seeking a collaborative and confident Academic Quality Enhancement Officer to join our Academic Quality Enhancement Office on a part-time, fixed-term basis until 30 November 2027. This is an opportunity to help contribute to enhancement related projects aimed at maintaining academic standards, supporting effective quality assurance and contribute to a cycle of continuous academic enhancement across the University and its partners. The role Working closely with Schools, professional services and partners, you will provide clear advice, guidance, monitoring and oversight across a broad range of academic quality enhancement activities. You will help colleagues apply the University’s academic regulatory and quality assurance frameworks consistently and effectively to support student outcome improvements. Your main responsibilities will include: • Supporting the curriculum development, validation and review cycle, academic assurance, external examining, audit and other quality-related activity; • Providing authoritative advice and guidance on academic regulations, policies, procedures and the maintenance of academic standards; • Contributing to the review and enhancement of academic quality practices, processes and guidance, informed by sector developments and external expectations; • Coordinating quality-related management information, reports and committee activity within required timescales; • Supporting collaborative provision and partnerships, including due diligence, approval, monitoring, review and annual reporting; and • Sharing good practice, supporting staff development and, where required, overseeing the work of administrative colleagues. About you You will bring experience of working with academic enhancement environments, higher education regulations or quality processes in a complex organisation, together with the judgement and confidence to provide accurate and practical advice. You will be able to build constructive relationships with a wide range of colleagues and partners, manage competing priorities and communicate complex information clearly in writing and in person. Closing date: Friday 13th November 2026 (23:59) To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Dominic Ramsden at D.B.Ramsden@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
