    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=217640OCC8&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Law",
      "description": "Job profile skip to job profile skip to job details Search for job Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job details Job reference REQ0002160 Date posted 23/09/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 20/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£44,746 - £50,253) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Lecturer candidate pack REQ00021.pdf Lecturer in Law Job description We are a modern, professional university with a dedicated and diverse community. Our vision is to be an excellent, accessible, globally engaged university contributing positively to a thriving northern economy. Our mission is to ensure we use our knowledge and resources to make a positive and decisive difference to people, communities and organisations. We are a community of around 23,000 students from over 140 countries and 2,200 staff, and our history dates to the founding of Leeds Mechanics Institute in 1824. We are a major organisation in our region, and the University contributes many millions of pounds to the local economy each year. Our Law School sits in the heart of the great city of Leeds, the most important legal centre outside London and home to over 200 law firms employing more than 10,000 professionals. It is perfectly placed to ensure all our undergraduate, postgraduate, full and part-time students can access the wealth of practical experience and employment opportunities available on our doorstep. We work closely with employers and partners to help our graduates become ready for work, ready for life and ready to seize all the opportunities that lie ahead. This is strengthened by our commitment to student success, innovation, enterprise, global reach and strong local impact in an increasingly competitive Higher Education environment. We are investing in our academic provision and wish to appoint an inspiring and enthusiastic individual to join our team as Lecturer. We expect all our staff to contribute to our teaching provision and deliver a high-quality student experience and to publish. Candidates for the Lecturer role should either hold a UK legal professional qualification with relevant experience or be qualified to doctoral level. The successful candidate will also hold a UK undergraduate law degree or GDL (CPE), and a master’s qualification. The successful candidate will have experience of teaching and learning in an HE or equivalent setting and demonstrate a commitment to research and publication. We expect all our staff to contribute to our provision and help deliver a high-quality student experience. The successful candidate will be expected to teach at both undergraduate and postgraduate level and should have experience of teaching at least one of the Foundations of Legal Knowledge. Preference will be given to those candidates who can deliver teaching in one or more of the following are: Applied Corporate Law Business Law Company Law Commercial Law Corporate Secretarial Practice European Law in Context Family and Child Law Legal Tech Closing date: Tuesday 20th October 2026 (23:59) Interviews will take place during November and will be conducted online. There will be a process of longlisting. All longlisted applicants will be invited to submit a recorded teaching session, for example a narrated PowerPoint presentation, for shortlisting purposes and before interviews takes place. If you would like to discuss this post informally contact Melissa Askew, Head of Law (Undergraduate) by email at law@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . With 38 days’ annual leave, generous pension contributions, and a supportive, collegial environment, this role offers the chance to make a significant contribution to the continued success and growth of Leeds Law School. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from women and black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Job title Lecturer in Law Job reference REQ0002160 Date posted 23/09/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 20/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£44,746 - £50,253) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Lecturer candidate pack REQ00021.pdf Job description We are a modern, professional university with a dedicated and diverse community. Our vision is to be an excellent, accessible, globally engaged university contributing positively to a thriving northern economy. Our mission is to ensure we use our knowledge and resources to make a positive and decisive difference to people, communities and organisations. We are a community of around 23,000 students from over 140 countries and 2,200 staff, and our history dates to the founding of Leeds Mechanics Institute in 1824. We are a major organisation in our region, and the University contributes many millions of pounds to the local economy each year. Our Law School sits in the heart of the great city of Leeds, the most important legal centre outside London and home to over 200 law firms employing more than 10,000 professionals. It is perfectly placed to ensure all our undergraduate, postgraduate, full and part-time students can access the wealth of practical experience and employment opportunities available on our doorstep. We work closely with employers and partners to help our graduates become ready for work, ready for life and ready to seize all the opportunities that lie ahead. This is strengthened by our commitment to student success, innovation, enterprise, global reach and strong local impact in an increasingly competitive Higher Education environment. We are investing in our academic provision and wish to appoint an inspiring and enthusiastic individual to join our team as Lecturer. We expect all our staff to contribute to our teaching provision and deliver a high-quality student experience and to publish. Candidates for the Lecturer role should either hold a UK legal professional qualification with relevant experience or be qualified to doctoral level. The successful candidate will also hold a UK undergraduate law degree or GDL (CPE), and a master’s qualification. The successful candidate will have experience of teaching and learning in an HE or equivalent setting and demonstrate a commitment to research and publication. We expect all our staff to contribute to our provision and help deliver a high-quality student experience. The successful candidate will be expected to teach at both undergraduate and postgraduate level and should have experience of teaching at least one of the Foundations of Legal Knowledge. Preference will be given to those candidates who can deliver teaching in one or more of the following are: Applied Corporate Law Business Law Company Law Commercial Law Corporate Secretarial Practice European Law in Context Family and Child Law Legal Tech Closing date: Tuesday 20th October 2026 (23:59) Interviews will take place during November and will be conducted online. There will be a process of longlisting. All longlisted applicants will be invited to submit a recorded teaching session, for example a narrated PowerPoint presentation, for shortlisting purposes and before interviews takes place. If you would like to discuss this post informally contact Melissa Askew, Head of Law (Undergraduate) by email at law@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . With 38 days’ annual leave, generous pension contributions, and a supportive, collegial environment, this role offers the chance to make a significant contribution to the continued success and growth of Leeds Law School. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from women and black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Send to a friend Apply online"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=615918O3Ag&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Occupational Health Advisor (Part-time)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Mon, 12 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002155 Date posted 08/09/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 30/10/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 (£39,906 - £44,746 pro rata) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ2155.pdf Occupational Health Advisor (Part-time) Job description Permanent | Part-time (15 - 22.5 hours per week) | Hybrid working Help create a healthy, supportive workplace where people can thrive. At Leeds Beckett University, our people make an extraordinary difference every day. From teaching and research to professional services, every colleague plays an important part in creating an outstanding experience for our students and communities. That's why looking after the health and wellbeing of our colleagues matters. We're looking for an experienced Occupational Health Advisor to join our HR team. This is an opportunity to use your professional expertise to support colleagues at every stage of their working lives, helping people stay healthy, return to work safely and feel supported when they need it most. If you're passionate about workplace health, enjoy building trusted relationships and want to be part of a collaborative and values-led team, we'd love to hear from you. The difference you'll make As our Occupational Health Advisor, you'll provide professional, evidence-based advice that helps colleagues and managers make informed decisions about health at work. No two days are the same. You'll manage occupational health referrals, advise on fitness for work, workplace adjustments and rehabilitation, and support managers with complex attendance and wellbeing matters. You'll balance sound clinical judgement with empathy, helping colleagues feel listened to, respected and supported throughout their experience. You'll also help shape how occupational health develops at Leeds Beckett. Whether it's identifying wellbeing trends, contributing to health promotion initiatives or working alongside HR colleagues to continuously improve our service, you'll play an important role in creating a healthy, inclusive workplace where everyone can succeed. What you'll bring You'll be a Registered Nurse with current NMC registration and a recognised Occupational Health qualification, together with a commitment to continuing professional development. You'll have experience delivering occupational health services in a complex organisation and be confident managing a varied caseload involving sensitive and sometimes challenging situations. Just as importantly, you'll be someone who enjoys working with people. You'll be approachable, compassionate and able to build credibility quickly, communicating with confidence while treating every colleague with professionalism, care and respect. We're particularly interested in hearing from people who have experience of: occupational health assessments and management referrals sickness absence management and workplace rehabilitation advising on reasonable adjustments and fitness for work health surveillance across complex organisations with diverse roles interpreting occupational health legislation and professional guidance maintaining accurate confidential clinical records and using occupational health systems promoting workplace wellbeing and developing health initiatives working collaboratively with HR colleagues and managers to achieve positive outcomes. Why Leeds Beckett? Working here means being part of a welcoming, ambitious university where everyone is encouraged to contribute, develop and make a positive difference. We know that looking after our colleagues enables them to do their best work, so we're committed to creating an environment where you can thrive too. In return, we offer: flexible and hybrid working generous annual leave entitlement an excellent pension scheme ongoing learning and professional development reduced tuition fees subsidised sports and fitness facilities a comprehensive range of wellbeing and employee benefits. Our HR team is based at our Headingley Campus. This role offers hybrid working, with a combination of home and campus working. Attendance on campus will be required for meetings, collaborative working and occasional in-person clinical appointments. We are flexible about working patterns, although a minimum commitment of 15 hours per week is required. Closing Date: Friday 30th October 2026 (23.59) Interview date: Wednesday 14th October, in person at Headingley campus (this may be subject to change) Creating a more inclusive university At Leeds Beckett University, we're committed to creating a diverse and inclusive community where everyone feels they belong. We welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates and particularly encourage applications from Black and Global Majority ethnic candidates, who are currently under-represented at this level within the University. We're committed to making our recruitment process as inclusive as possible and will make reasonable adjustments wherever needed to support candidates throughout the application and interview process. Ready to apply? We review applications as they're received and may close this vacancy once we've received sufficient applications. If you're interested, we'd encourage you to apply as soon as possible. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=118517OR0M&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Accounting & Finance (0.4FTE)",
      "description": "Job profile skip to job profile skip to job details Search for job Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job details Job reference REQ0002183 Date posted 16/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 11/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£45,641 - £51,258 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002183.pdf Lecturer in Accounting & Finance (0.4FTE) Job description Leeds Business School’s vision is to be an excellent, accessible, innovative and engaged Business School contributing positively to the regional economy. We are looking for a Lecturer (0.4 FTE) in Accounting & Finance, who can make a significant contribution to our undergraduate and postgraduate professionally accredited courses. You will be an established academic in accounting & finance with experience in teaching management accounting, financial accounting and financial management. You will also make an active contribution to professional engagement and pursue high-quality research in the subject area. The Accounting and Finance subject group has a long history of applied learning and engagement with the business community, and we are looking for candidates with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and innovative approach to delivering the curriculum.  You will have a strong commitment to ensuring an outstanding student experience, which is focussed on achieving high levels of employability and a good record of research in the Accounting or Finance. Closing date: Wednesday 11 November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Job title Lecturer in Accounting & Finance (0.4FTE) Job reference REQ0002183 Date posted 16/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 11/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£45,641 - £51,258 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002183.pdf Job description Leeds Business School’s vision is to be an excellent, accessible, innovative and engaged Business School contributing positively to the regional economy. We are looking for a Lecturer (0.4 FTE) in Accounting & Finance, who can make a significant contribution to our undergraduate and postgraduate professionally accredited courses. You will be an established academic in accounting & finance with experience in teaching management accounting, financial accounting and financial management. You will also make an active contribution to professional engagement and pursue high-quality research in the subject area. The Accounting and Finance subject group has a long history of applied learning and engagement with the business community, and we are looking for candidates with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and innovative approach to delivering the curriculum.  You will have a strong commitment to ensuring an outstanding student experience, which is focussed on achieving high levels of employability and a good record of research in the Accounting or Finance. Closing date: Wednesday 11 November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Send to a friend Apply online"
