have experience of managing diaries and schedules for senior managers, servicing and minuting meetings, coordinating activity and dealing with a wide range of correspondence and information. You will be confident working across a large or complex organisation and will ideally have experience of supporting areas such as business operations, finance, human resources, strategic planning, compliance, risk or quality management. You will have excellent written and verbal communication skills and the ability to prepare reports, briefings and complex correspondence accurately and to a high standard. Excellent IT skills are essential, including experience of Microsoft Office, bespoke databases and AI tools. You will be comfortable learning and using new systems and will look for opportunities to improve the way administrative services are delivered. You will be able to organise and prioritise your own workload, work to deadlines and respond positively to changing priorities. You will have a proactive approach, be able to use your initiative and always maintain confidentiality and discretion. Above all, you will be a flexible and collaborative team member who is committed to providing a high-quality service to colleagues and stakeholders. Working here Working at Leeds Beckett University means joining a diverse and supportive community where you can develop your skills and make a difference. This is a hybrid role, working across 5 days with a minimum of 3 days on Campus. Closing date: Monday 2nd November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Send to a friend Apply online"
