    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=247934OQQ0&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Space Supervisor",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Fri, 16 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002181 Date posted 15/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 02/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 5 (£35,302 - £39,560) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002181.pdf Space Supervisor Job description Leeds Beckett University is seeking an organised, proactive and customer-focused Space Supervisor to join our Estates and Facilities team. This is an exciting opportunity to play a key role in managing and improving the University’s physical estate. You will support the Space Manager in the effective planning, monitoring and management of space, furniture, signage and associated records across the University. You will lead and coordinate office moves, migrations and space-related projects, working closely with colleagues, contractors, consultants and other stakeholders to deliver high-quality outcomes with minimal disruption. As Space Supervisor, you will also project manage space-related works from inception to completion, including space planning, furniture, signage, minor refurbishment and associated operational activities. The role will involve managing the procurement, maintenance and lifecycle of furniture assets; acting as contract lead for furniture, signage and migration-related suppliers; and monitoring performance, quality, compliance and value for money. You will coordinate University signage projects, organise room utilisation and space surveys, analyse findings and provide recommendations to inform operational and strategic planning. You will also maintain accurate records relating to space, furniture, signage and associated assets, produce reliable space management data and reports, and provide professional advice on space management, utilisation, furniture standards, signage, procedures and health and safety requirements. In addition, you will supervise and coordinate the work of the Space Coordinator, supporting the effective delivery of day-to-day operational activities while promoting high standards of customer service, sustainability, compliance and continuous improvement. We are seeking someone with a degree in a related area or equivalent relevant experience with previous experience of project management who has a strong commitment to customer service with excellent communication and negotiation skills with the ability to work flexibly and collaboratively as part of a team. This is an opportunity to make a visible contribution to the University environment, helping to create effective, inclusive and sustainable spaces that support students, staff and visitors. You will work across a varied portfolio of projects and operational activities, collaborating with colleagues at all levels and helping to shape the future use of the University estate. This is a hybrid working role, with an expectation of a minimum of 3 days on Campus. Closing date: Monday 2nd November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=280369OQTe&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Commercial and Operations Analytical Lead (KTP)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Fri, 16 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002182 Date posted 15/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 19/11/2026 Location Blank Salary £36,000 - £40,000 dependent on skills and experience Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support, Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002182.pdf Commercial and Operations Analytical Lead (KTP) Job description We are looking for a motivated and curious individual to lead an exciting Knowledge Transfer Partnership (KTP) project in collaboration with Arville Textiles Ltd, an innovative, forward-thinking industry-leading specialist manufacturer of advanced textile solutions, known for their agility, expertise and customer-centric approach. This 30-month project offers a unique opportunity to work closely with Arville, based in their Headquarters in Wetherby, and a supportive, cross-disciplinary academic team from Leeds Beckett. Together, you will embed a Commercial and Operational Transformation Strategy, connecting commercial insight with operational priorities, helping Arville make better, faster decisions that support margin-led, sustainable growth. We encourage applications from a self-starter with excellent project management and communication skills, who comes with a strong background in business analytics, process improvement or digital marketing. Building connections amongst a dynamic team at Arville will set the project for success, so evidencing a proactive, agile approach with a willingness to learn is important for the project delivery. About Arville Textiles Ltd Established in 1951 as a family-owned business, Arville has built a world-wide reputation in their advanced technical textiles sector for expertise, experience and quality. They work in partnership with large multinationals and significant specialist companies across global OEM supply chains, including defence, aerospace and automative sectors. The Person This is a unique role spanning commercial and operational optimisation, necessarily underpinned by change management to embed new ways of working. As such, applicants need to demonstrate the ability to balance structured thinking with flexibility and responsiveness to change. The role will also require excellent project management skills, data analysis with the ability to lead and drive objectives through strong interpersonal skills and effective stakeholder engagement. If you would like to find out more about this role we plan to hold an online information session on Teams Eventbrite link is here: Arville Information Session Closing date: Thursday 19th November 2026 (23:59) We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=296550OVRr&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Course Administrator (Fixed Term to 30/11/2027)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002192 Date posted 22/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 27/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 3 (£26,615 - £30,986) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate pack REQ2192.pdf Course Administrator (Fixed Term to 30/11/2027) Job description We have an exciting temporary opportunity in the School of Humanities and Social Sciences; we are looking to appoint a pro-active and enthusiastic Course Administrator on a temporary basis (until 30th November 2027), to cover a period of maternity leave. The postholder will provide efficient administrative support for courses and work closely with academic colleagues to ensure a positive student experience throughout the whole of the student journey. Duties will include proactive management of course administration, acting as a key contact point for students and the course team. Maintaining and updating localised and centralised records, organising and servicing of meetings and compiling reports. The successful candidate will possess high level spreadsheet, database and word processing skills; the ability to keep accurate records; excellent communication skills and a drive to provide outstanding customer service. They will also be able to prioritise workloads under pressure and demonstrate a flexible approach to work. The role is based at City Campus and is suitable for a mixture of on campus and hybrid working. Working arrangements are dependent on the job role, team and University requirements and will be discussed with candidates at interview. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Elizabeth Kijewski at e.kijewski@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Friday 27th November 2026 (23:59) Please be advised that due to the minimum salary thresholds imposed by the UKVI, this post will not qualify for university sponsorship for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. You must have the right to work in the UK to apply for this vacancy. Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
