      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002191 Date posted 22/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 20/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 3 (£26,615 - £30,986) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support, Professional/Managerial Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002191.pdf Secretary FTC until 31/07/2027 Job description The Carnegie School of Sport is seeking a dedicated and proactive secretary to join our School office. This role is pivotal in supporting our school office to deliver a customer focussed and supportive service to all colleagues and stakeholders. Candidates should have good administrative experience and excellent written and oral communication skills, possessing high level IT skills, and should be 'customer focused' with a friendly and positive attitude. Working within a busy team, the post holder will need to be able to organise and prioritise their own workload, exercise initiative and work well under pressure. If you want to make a difference and feel you have the skills to make this role your own, please apply via the link below, detailing your experience and giving examples of where you have met the employee specification, in particular the performance attributes as noted in the Job Description. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Nicola Queenan, School Manager at N.Queenan@leedsbeckett.ac.uk Closing Date: Friday 20th November 2026 at 23:29 Interview date: Friday 11th December 2026 (this may be subject to change) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=692134OVRr&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Research Officer (Fixed term 1 year)",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002193 Date posted 22/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 05/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 5 (£35,302 - £39,560) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002193.pdf Research Officer (Fixed term 1 year) Job description The School of Humanities and Social Sciences (HSS) is committed to making a positive and decisive difference to people, organisations and communities through excellent education and research. We are increasingly recognised locally, nationally and globally as an outstanding department that supports its diverse student community to achieve excellent outcomes, and that generates original impactful research. HSS has a highly applied, collaborative research culture which is supported by our research centres (School of Humanities and Social Sciences | Leeds Beckett University). To support our REF 2029 submission for Unit 28 (History), with a particular focus on developing and recording the impact of our research, we are seeking to appoint a Research Officer to work with colleagues on the following projects: Forged by Fire (with Professor Shane Ewen): https://www.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/research/centre-for-culture-and-humanities/forged-by-fire/ War on Waste (with Dr Henry Irving): https://www.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/research/centre-for-culture-and-humanities/war-on-waste/ Successful candidates will work with the REF unit lead for History (Prof. Ewen) and the Director of Research to support ongoing research projects. For an informal discussion speak to Professor Ewen s.ewen@leedsbeckett.ac.uk ; tel: (0113) 812 3340. Closing date: Friday 5th November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer . Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=024550OUIl&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Information Governance Officer",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002190 Date posted 21/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 22/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 5 (£35,302 - £39,560) Package Please refer to candidate pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ2190.pdf Information Governance Officer Job description Are you passionate about information rights, transparency and protecting personal data? Join our Information Governance team and play a key role in helping Leeds Beckett University meet its legal and regulatory responsibilities. You'll manage Freedom of Information, Environmental Information Regulations and Data Protection requests, provide practical advice to colleagues, support records management activities and help promote a culture of accountability and good governance across the University. This is a varied role that offers the opportunity to work with colleagues from across the institution, tackle complex challenges and make a real impact on how information is managed and protected. About You We're looking for someone who: Has experience of handling information rights requests and data protection matters. Understands Freedom of Information, UK GDPR and Data Protection legislation. Can analyse complex information and confidently apply legislation and exemptions. Has excellent written and verbal communication skills and can explain technical issues clearly. Is organised, proactive and able to manage competing priorities. Enjoys building positive working relationships and delivering high-quality customer service. Has a relevant qualification or equivalent experience in information governance, data protection or a related field. Why Join Us? This is an excellent opportunity to develop your career in information governance within a supportive and collaborative team. You'll have the chance to broaden your expertise across FOI, Data Protection and Records Management while contributing to an organisation that values transparency, integrity and continuous improvement. If you're looking for a role where your knowledge and judgement can make a real difference, we'd love to hear from you. This role operates on a hybrid working model, combining on-campus presence, at Headingley and City Campus, and flexibility to work from home. Working arrangements are dependent on the job role, team and University requirements and will be discussed with candidates at interview. Closing date: Wednesday 22nd November (23.59) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=513673OTZv&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Learning Support Officer",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002188 Date posted 20/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 23/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,986 - £35,302) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002188.pdf Learning Support Officer Job description We are looking for a practical, organised and approachable Learning Support Officer to support teaching, student learning and research in Psychology. Working with academic colleagues, Principal Learning Officers and other professional services staff, you will help students and staff make effective and safe use of our specialist facilities, equipment, software and learning resources. You will also have a role supporting administration of our Speech and Language Therapy Clinic. This is a varied, hands-on role. You will support practical classes and research projects, provide demonstrations and guidance, help administer learning and clinical spaces and ethics processes, and contribute to open days and other student recruitment activity. You will also help maintain equipment, records and procedures so that our facilities remain safe, well organised and ready for use. About Us Psychology at Leeds Beckett University is known for its impactful education and research. Through our undergraduate and postgraduate programs, we aim to make a meaningful difference to individuals and communities. Our collaborative culture, supported by the Centre for Psychological Research (PsyCen) fosters original, applied research. For more about our Psychology Group, visit Psychology at Leeds Beckett . Key Responsibilities • Provide high-level technical and administrative support for teaching, research, and consultancy within the Psychology Subject Group. • Maintain laboratory facilities and ensure equipment safety, repair and availability. • Contribute to curriculum development and student recruitment activities. • Collaborate with academic staff to develop and maintain technical resources, operating procedures and data management systems. • Provide administrative support for our speech and language therapy clinic What We’re Looking For We’re seeking a highly skilled professional with: • A degree or vocational qualification in Psychology or related fields (or equivalent experience). • Experience with psychology laboratory equipment and/ or relevant software. • Strong interpersonal, learning support, administrative and technical skills. • A commitment to providing a safe and inclusive learning environment. Why Join Us? At Leeds Beckett, we value your growth. We provide: •  Professional development and training opportunities. •  A collaborative and inclusive community. • Competitive salary and benefits, including 28 days of annual leave       (increasing to 31 with service). Closing date: Monday 23rd November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
