      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Job profile skip to job profile skip to job details Search for job Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job details Job reference REQ0002184 Date posted 19/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 13/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 7 (£45,641 - £51,258) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002184.pdf Lecturer Job description Leeds Business School vision is to be an excellent, accessible, innovative and engaged Business School contributing positively to the regional economy. Our business courses, including our degree apprenticeships are very successful and popular, resulting in a significant opportunity for us to increase and enrich our Business Strategy, Operations and Enterprise team in the Business School. The Subject Group has a long history of applied learning and engagement with business practitioners, and we are seeking candidates who have relevant business experience and also possess teaching experience with an emphasis on Artificial Intelligence and Data Analytics within Business and Management, including practical and analytical methods, Responsible AI adoption and Business Process Management.. The successful candidate would contribute to a number of programmes, pathways and modules within our curriculum but particularly our new MSc Management and AI course. You will have a strong commitment to ensuring an outstanding student experience, which is focussed on helping to equip our learners with the skills needed to achieve high levels of employability. To arrange an informal discussion about this post,