    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=215540OSfb&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Communications and Campaigns Officer",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002185 Date posted 19/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 02/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 4 (£30,986 - £35,302) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002185.pdf Communications and Campaigns Officer Job description Are you a creative communicator with a passion for storytelling and digital content? Join our Communications and Campaigns team at Leeds Beckett University, where your work can inspire change, support students, and bring impactful research to life. We're looking for someone with experience in content creation, media, social media, PR and digital communications - someone who thrives in a fast-paced environment and has a great eye for a story. This role involves developing campaigns to connect with diverse audiences, translating complex research into compelling news stories, supporting press office activity, contributing to media coverage, and helping shape the university's voice across digital and traditional channels. It’s a hands-on position where your skills will support high-profile campaigns, celebrate student success, promote research, and drive engagement. From writing news stories, features and social media content, capturing and editing video and managing content calendars, to live-posting at our events and responding to emerging stories, you’ll be part of a busy, creative, and supportive team. If you bring great writing skills, a strong awareness of social media trends, an understanding of what makes content engaging and a collaborative mindset, we’d love to hear from you. At Leeds Beckett, we value diverse perspectives and offer hybrid working, generous holidays, and career development support. Join a team committed to meaningful communications that make a difference. Closing date: Monday 2nd November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=958264OSvw&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Course Administrator",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Tue, 27 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002186 Date posted 19/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 20/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 3 (£26,615 - £30,986) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002186.pdf Course Administrator Job description Are you an experienced, highly motivated, Administrator looking for a new challenge? If yes, we are seeking to appoint a full-time permanent Course Administrator to join our Professional Services Team within the School of Health. You will be joining our highly supportive team, with a hybrid working arrangement of some on campus working along with some remote working from home. The post holder will be required to provide efficient and effective administrative support for a suite of courses, working closely with our academic colleagues to ensure our students/apprentices receive a positive experience throughout their journey at Leeds Beckett. The role includes acting as the key contact point for students/apprentices, course teams and external stakeholders on all course related matters. Providing proactive management of course administration, maintaining and updating records, organising and servicing of meetings and compiling of reports. The successful candidate will be a highly motivated individual, with a high level of IT skills, with experience of using a range of the Microsoft Packages such as Word and Excel. A high level of organisational and administrative skills, excellent verbal and written communication skills along with the ability to work without supervision. At Leeds Beckett we are committed to providing an excellent learning environment for our students along with a stimulating work environment for our colleagues, where everyone contributes to our success. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Tracy Gray at T.Gray@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Friday 20th November 2026 (23:59) Please be advised that due to the minimum salary thresholds imposed by the UKVI, this post will not qualify for university sponsorship for new applicants to the Skilled Worker visa route. You must have the right to work in the UK to apply for this vacancy. Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=629551OYnr&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Academic Quality Enhancement Officer",
      "description": "Job profile . undefined undefined Wk Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri Sat Sun NaN Today is Wed, 28 Oct 2026 skip to job profile skip to job details Leeds Beckett Home Search for job Search for job Working here Application guide Living here Support for International Colleagues Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job reference REQ0002195 Date posted 28/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 20/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 (£40,704 - £45,641) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Administrative/Support Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002195.pdf Academic Quality Enhancement Officer Job description Shape and strengthen academic quality at Leeds Beckett University We are seeking a collaborative and confident Academic Quality Enhancement Officer to join our Academic Quality Enhancement Office. This is an opportunity to help maintain academic standards, support effective quality assurance and contribute to continuous enhancement across the University and its partners. The role Working closely with Schools, professional services and partners, you will provide clear advice, guidance, monitoring and oversight across a broad range of academic quality activities. You will help colleagues apply the University’s academic regulatory and quality assurance frameworks consistently and effectively. Your main responsibilities will include: • supporting the validation and review cycle, academic assurance, external examining, audit and other quality-related activity; • providing authoritative advice and guidance on academic regulations, policies, procedures and the maintenance of academic standards; • contributing to the review and enhancement of academic quality policies, processes and guidance, informed by sector developments and external expectations; • co-ordinating quality-related management information, reports and committee activity within required timescales; • supporting collaborative provision and partnerships, including due diligence, approval, monitoring, review and annual reporting; and • sharing good practice, supporting staff development and, where required, overseeing the work of administrative colleagues. About you You will bring experience of working with policies, regulations or quality processes in a complex organisation, together with the judgement and confidence to provide accurate and practical advice. You will be able to build constructive relationships with a wide range of colleagues and partners, manage competing priorities and communicate complex information clearly in writing and in person. To arrange an informal discussion about this post, please contact Dominic Ramsden at D.B.Ramsden@leedsbeckett.ac.uk . Closing date: Friday 20th November 2026 (23:59) Interview date: Thursday 10th December 2026 (this may be subject to change) Working here means you’ll also have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend +44 (0) 113 812 0000 Find us Accessibility Disclaimer Privacy Modern Slavery Statement Contact Us A member of University Alliance © 2026 Leeds Beckett University"
    },
    "https://vacancies.leedsbeckett.ac.uk/ce0984li_webrecruitment/wrd/run/ETREC107GF.open?VACANCY_ID=206684OZ5G&WVID=7412577lKO&LANG=USA": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (30 hours, fixed term",
      "description": "Job profile skip to job profile skip to job details Search for job Existing user login Forgotten password My applications My profile Job profile The job requirements are detailed below. Where applicable the skills, qualifications and memberships required for this job have also been included. The Further Details for each job are in PDF format and you will need Adobe Acrobat in order to view these. To download a free version, please click on the image below. Job details Job details Job reference REQ0002196 Date posted 28/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 16/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 (£40,704 - £45,641 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002196.pdf Research Fellow (30 hours, fixed term - 12 months) Job description Leeds Beckett University is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Research Fellow to join a multidisciplinary research team undertaking an externally funded systematic review of interventions for fathers and male carers experiencing multiple and complex needs. Funded by Foundations, this 12-month project will identify what works, for whom and under what conditions, to inform the development of evidence-based support for fathers, male carers and their families. Working across the Carnegie School of Education, School of Health, and School of Social Sciences and Humanities, you will contribute to a systematic review that will inform a subsequent practice review and generate recommendations for professionals working with families experiencing multiple and complex needs. The findings will strengthen the evidence base on parenting support and help inform the development and delivery of interventions that better respond to the needs of fathers, male carers and their families. About you We are looking for a researcher with experience of conducting or contributing to systematic reviews or other evidence synthesis projects, a strong eye for detail and a commitment to producing high-quality research. You will have excellent organisational skills and the ability to work accurately and methodically with research evidence. You will be confident working independently and collaboratively, managing competing priorities and contributing effectively to the delivery of a time-limited research project. An interest in parenting support, family interventions and the experiences of fathers and male carers with multiple and complex needs would be particularly welcome. About the team You will work within a supportive, multidisciplinary team led by Dr Nicole Gridley from the Carnegie School of Education and Professor Sharon Vincent from the School of Health. The project brings together expertise across education, health and social sciences and humanities to address an important area of family support research. Why join us? This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to research with clear potential to inform professional practice and improve support for fathers, male carers and their families. You will have the opportunity to develop your evidence synthesis expertise, work collaboratively with researchers across disciplines, and contribute to translating research findings into practical recommendations for professionals working with families experiencing multiple and complex needs. If you are an organised and thoughtful researcher who is passionate about high-quality evidence and its application to policy and practice, we would welcome your application. Closing date: Monday 16th November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Job title Research Fellow (30 hours, fixed term - 12 months) Job reference REQ0002196 Date posted 28/10/2026 Application closing date: Midnight 16/11/2026 Location Leeds Salary Grade 6 (£40,704 - £45,641 pro rata) Package Please refer to Candidate Pack Job category/type Academic/Research Attachments Candidate Pack REQ0002196.pdf Job description Leeds Beckett University is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Research Fellow to join a multidisciplinary research team undertaking an externally funded systematic review of interventions for fathers and male carers experiencing multiple and complex needs. Funded by Foundations, this 12-month project will identify what works, for whom and under what conditions, to inform the development of evidence-based support for fathers, male carers and their families. Working across the Carnegie School of Education, School of Health, and School of Social Sciences and Humanities, you will contribute to a systematic review that will inform a subsequent practice review and generate recommendations for professionals working with families experiencing multiple and complex needs. The findings will strengthen the evidence base on parenting support and help inform the development and delivery of interventions that better respond to the needs of fathers, male carers and their families. About you We are looking for a researcher with experience of conducting or contributing to systematic reviews or other evidence synthesis projects, a strong eye for detail and a commitment to producing high-quality research. You will have excellent organisational skills and the ability to work accurately and methodically with research evidence. You will be confident working independently and collaboratively, managing competing priorities and contributing effectively to the delivery of a time-limited research project. An interest in parenting support, family interventions and the experiences of fathers and male carers with multiple and complex needs would be particularly welcome. About the team You will work within a supportive, multidisciplinary team led by Dr Nicole Gridley from the Carnegie School of Education and Professor Sharon Vincent from the School of Health. The project brings together expertise across education, health and social sciences and humanities to address an important area of family support research. Why join us? This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to research with clear potential to inform professional practice and improve support for fathers, male carers and their families. You will have the opportunity to develop your evidence synthesis expertise, work collaboratively with researchers across disciplines, and contribute to translating research findings into practical recommendations for professionals working with families experiencing multiple and complex needs. If you are an organised and thoughtful researcher who is passionate about high-quality evidence and its application to policy and practice, we would welcome your application. Closing date: Monday 16th November 2026 (23:59) Working here means you’ll have access to a wide range of benefits including our generous pension schemes, excellent holiday entitlements, flexible working, reduced study fees, subsidised fitness facilities and a lot more. We welcome applications from all individuals and particularly from black and minority ethnic candidates as members of these groups are currently under-represented at this level of post. All appointments will be based on merit. Leeds Beckett University is a Disability Confident Employer. Disabled candidates who demonstrate all essential criteria within the Person Specification will be invited to an interview. Apply online Send to a friend Send to a friend Apply online"
